<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Where Decor Belongs on a Kitchen Counter</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Before you add anything, decide which parts of the counter are for working and which are for styling. The National Kitchen &amp; Bath Association’s <a href="https://kb.nkba.org/uploads/2022/05/Kitchen-Planning-Guidelines.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kitchen Planning Guidelines</a> recommend a section of continuous countertop at least 36 inches wide and 24 inches deep right next to the sink as the main prep area, plus at least 12 inches of landing area on one side of the cooktop and 15 inches on the other. Those are the spots to keep clear.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">That leaves the corners, the back edge along the backsplash and the ends of the counter run for decor. Styled pieces there catch the eye without getting in the way of chopping, serving or setting down a hot pan.</p>



